{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.6,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_component_type",
      "components": ["U4 (STM32L476RGT6, top-edge supply pins)", "six 10k resistors in series with VCC"],
      "pins": ["U4.1 (VBAT)", "U4.19 (VDD)", "U4.32 (VDD)", "U4.48 (VDD)", "U4.64 (VDDUSB)"],
      "nets": ["VCC", "U4 supply pins (each isolated from VCC by a 10k resistor)"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet (PCB.kicad_sch) the VCC arrow drops onto a horizontal rail, and from that rail hang six red '10k' resistor symbols (same resistor glyph/value style as R7) that connect in series between VCC and the MCU's top-edge power pins (VBAT/VDD/VDDUSB). The VDD pins are therefore not directly on the VCC rail; each is fed through 10 kΩ.",
      "expected": "The MCU's VBAT/VDD/VDDUSB pins must be tied directly to the VCC rail, with decoupling capacitance from VCC to GND. The specification's power section states the bypass parts 'only attach to the shared rails' and that VCC 'is only consumed' by the MCU — i.e. the supply pins sit on VCC with no series element. A 10 kΩ series resistor on a supply pin is never correct.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Root sheet, top of U4: VCC arrow -> horizontal wire -> six red '10k' resistor symbols -> MCU VBAT/VDD/VDDUSB pins (resistor glyph identical to R7; capacitor values elsewhere are drawn blue two-line symbols, e.g. the 'Decoupling Capacitors' block)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "§4: 'Decoupling / bulk capacitance directly on VCC–GND (all generic bypass, cannot be tied to a specific pin from the netlist alone since they only attach to the shared rails)' and 'The schematic does not show where VCC is generated; it is only consumed.'"}
      ],
      "impact": "Each MCU supply pin is fed through 10 kΩ instead of being hard-tied to VCC, so the chip sees a large voltage drop and almost no current, with no local decoupling. The MCU will fail to power up / brown out, taking the whole board (NFC, display, touch, SWD) down with it.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing shows the MCU's VBAT/VDD/VDDUSB pins connected to VCC through six series 10 kΩ resistors (red resistor glyphs), whereas the spec and standard practice require those supply pins to sit directly on the VCC rail with bypass caps to GND; this is the one supported anomaly. The reference-designator permutation (MCU shown as U4, NFC as U2, OLED as U1, etc.) is a naming/renumbering difference, not an electrical deviation, and is not reported."
}

